We can use many if statements and else if in order to try and meet a condition but we can use
switch instead.
so for example:
Chatter chatter;
switch(arg) { //does a correct string comparison (not reference comparison)
 case "echo";
    chatter = new EchoChatter(new String[] { "what "});
    break;
 case "other chatter";
    chatter = new OtherChatter();
    break;
 default:
    chatter = null;

}

this comes instead of if and else, the switch is more of cases that should happen when we want
to distinguish between multiple doable options. The break is necessary because if we don't
the switch will continue through all the cases and do all of them.

also you can't send reference to switch cases, so if we named echo some var and then sent it, it wouldn't work
only if its defined as a constant (private static final)

also you can enter multiple cases at once like "echo","Echo","ECHO"